{%- comment -%}
  Activity — one merged, reverse-chronological, typed stream of blog posts,
  notes (the `news` collection) and GitHub Releases (`site.data.activity`,
  generated by bin/activity-releases.js). Rendered on /activity/ and on the
  about page.

  Interface:
    include.limit — maximum rows to render. Omit for the full stream.

  The structure is deliberately two-part:

    (a) the ordering seam — produces `activity_items`, and nothing else
    (b) the render loop   — one branch per item type

  Keep sorting and limiting out of the render loop. The balance policy
  (per-source caps, then top-N; #163) belongs in (a). The release-summary
  override (#74, `_data/release_summaries.yml`) is resolved in the Release
  branch of (b), so it changes what a row says and never the order.

  Why (a) sorts keys, not items: posts and notes are Documents whose `date` is
  a Time, while a release is a hash from JSON whose `date` is an ISO 8601
  string. Jekyll's `sort: 'date'` compares a Time with a string correctly
  only because ActiveSupport, loaded by the plugins, redefines `Time#<=>`.
  Without it, Jekyll falls back to comparing the two as text and puts a
  release above a post or note from the same day, with no error (#168). So
  (a) does not depend on ActiveSupport: it builds one string key per item,
  `<epoch seconds, zero-padded to 12>|<source>|<index, zero-padded to 4>`,
  sorts the keys (every field is fixed width, so text order is chronological;
  the index pad assumes at most 9999 items per source), applies the limit, and
  resolves each key back to its object. Items in the same second order by
  source letter (release, post, note) and then by reverse position in their
  source: deterministic, but not meaningful.

  `date: '%s'` gives the same instant for a Time and for an ISO string with an
  explicit offset, whatever the build's timezone. Release dates always end in
  `Z`: bin/activity-releases.js writes them that way, and the guardrail in
  bin/activity-releases-refresh.sh rejects any other form.

  Type discrimination in (b): `item.collection` is `"news"` or `"posts"` for
  a Document. A release has no `collection`, so it is recognized by its own
  fields (`repo` and `tag`), and anything else is skipped rather than rendered
  as the wrong type. `inline` is consulted only within the Note branch.

  A release `summary` is plain text derived from upstream release notes, which
  anyone opening a PR upstream can influence: render it with `escape`, never
  `markdownify`. A hand-written override replaces it and is escaped the same
  way. The derived summary can be null; then the row shows the tag alone,
  unless an override applies. The `!= blank` guard depends on a `blank?`
  method that Liquid 4.0.4 does not define; the csl gem (pulled in by
  jekyll-scholar) supplies it.

  Real data cannot exercise the escaping, null-summary or same-day ordering
  paths, so after changing the seam (a), the Release branch of (b), or the
  gems those depend on, run `node bin/activity-fixture-check.js` (#168). It
  builds a copy of the site against the fixture in bin/fixtures/activity/.
  It is on demand, not in CI.

  There is no scroll container. Upstream's `<div class="table-responsive"
  style="max-height:60vw">` was a WCAG 2.1.1 failure (a scrollable region with
  no keyboard access); the about page bounds its own height with `limit`
  instead, and /activity/ is a full-length page like /blog/.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} (a) Ordering seam. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign activity_releases = site.data.activity.releases -%}
{%- assign activity_keys = '' | split: '' -%}
{%- for item in site.posts -%}
  {%- assign activity_pos = forloop.index0 | prepend: '0000' | slice: -4, 4 -%}
  {%- assign activity_key = item.date | date: '%s' | prepend: '000000000000' | slice: -12, 12 | append: '|p|' | append: activity_pos -%}
  {%- assign activity_keys = activity_keys | push: activity_key -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for item in site.news -%}
  {%- assign activity_pos = forloop.index0 | prepend: '0000' | slice: -4, 4 -%}
  {%- assign activity_key = item.date | date: '%s' | prepend: '000000000000' | slice: -12, 12 | append: '|n|' | append: activity_pos -%}
  {%- assign activity_keys = activity_keys | push: activity_key -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for item in activity_releases -%}
  {%- assign activity_pos = forloop.index0 | prepend: '0000' | slice: -4, 4 -%}
  {%- assign activity_key = item.date | date: '%s' | prepend: '000000000000' | slice: -12, 12 | append: '|r|' | append: activity_pos -%}
  {%- assign activity_keys = activity_keys | push: activity_key -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign activity_keys = activity_keys | sort | reverse -%}
{%- if include.limit and activity_keys.size > include.limit -%}
  {%- assign activity_keys = activity_keys | slice: 0, include.limit -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign activity_items = '' | split: '' -%}
{%- for activity_key in activity_keys -%}
  {%- assign activity_key_parts = activity_key | split: '|' -%}
  {%- comment -%} `split` yields strings, and Liquid indexes an array only by an Integer; `plus: 0` also drops the padding zeros. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign activity_index = activity_key_parts[2] | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- case activity_key_parts[1] -%}
    {%- when 'p' -%}
      {%- assign activity_items = activity_items | push: site.posts[activity_index] -%}
    {%- when 'n' -%}
      {%- assign activity_items = activity_items | push: site.news[activity_index] -%}
    {%- when 'r' -%}
      {%- assign activity_items = activity_items | push: activity_releases[activity_index] -%}
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} (b) Render loop. {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="activity">
  {%- if activity_items.size > 0 -%}
    <ul class="activity-list">
      {%- for item in activity_items -%}
        {%- if item.collection == 'news' -%}
          {%- assign item_type = 'note' -%}
          {%- assign item_type_label = 'Note' -%}
        {%- elsif item.collection == 'posts' -%}
          {%- assign item_type = 'post' -%}
          {%- assign item_type_label = 'Post' -%}
        {%- elsif item.repo and item.tag -%}
          {%- assign item_type = 'release' -%}
          {%- assign item_type_label = 'Release' -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- continue -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Posts and notes match the site's existing link convention (see
          latest_posts.liquid). A release always links out to its GitHub release
          page, and its branch below renders the new-tab attributes itself.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign item_external = false -%}
        {%- if item_type == 'release' -%}
          {%- assign item_href = item.url -%}
        {%- elsif item.redirect == blank -%}
          {%- assign item_href = item.url | relative_url -%}
        {%- elsif item.redirect contains '://' -%}
          {%- assign item_href = item.redirect -%}
          {%- assign item_external = true -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign item_href = item.redirect | relative_url -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        <li class="activity-item activity-item--{{ item_type }}">
          <div class="activity-meta">
            <time class="activity-date" datetime="{{ item.date | date_to_xmlschema }}">{{ item.date | date: '%s' | date: '%b %-d, %Y' }}</time>
            <span class="activity-type activity-type--{{ item_type }}">{{ item_type_label }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="activity-body">
            {%- if item_type == 'note' and item.inline -%}
              <p class="activity-note">{{ item.content | remove: '<p>' | remove: '</p>' | emojify }}</p>
            {%- elsif item_type == 'release' -%}
              <a class="activity-title" href="{{ item_href | escape }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                {{- item.repo | escape }}
                {{ item.tag | escape -}}
                <span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
              </a>
              {%- comment -%}
                Release-summary override (#74): a "repo@tag" entry in
                _data/release_summaries.yml replaces the derived summary. Keys
                match case-insensitively (an exact lookup would miss a miscased
                key silently, the #54 trap). A value YAML reads as null or
                false, or a blank one, falls back to the derived summary; the
                truthiness test comes before `strip`, which would turn false
                into the string "false".
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign item_summary = item.summary -%}
              {%- assign item_key = item.repo | append: '@' | append: item.tag | downcase -%}
              {%- for activity_override in site.data.release_summaries -%}
                {%- assign activity_override_key = activity_override[0] | downcase -%}
                {%- if activity_override_key == item_key -%}
                  {%- if activity_override[1] -%}
                    {%- assign activity_override_value = activity_override[1] | strip -%}
                    {%- if activity_override_value != '' -%}
                      {%- assign item_summary = activity_override_value -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- break -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- if item_summary != blank -%}
                <p class="activity-summary">{{ item_summary | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- else -%}
              <a
                class="activity-title"
                href="{{ item_href }}"
                {% if item_external %}
                  target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                {% endif %}
              >
                {{- item.title -}}
                {%- if item_external -%}
                  <span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>
              {%- if item_type == 'post' and item.categories.size > 0 -%}
                <ul class="activity-series">
                  {%- for category in item.categories -%}
                    <li>
                      <a href="{{ category | slugify | prepend: '/blog/category/' | relative_url }}">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-tag fa-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{ category }}
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  {%- else -%}
    <p class="activity-empty">Nothing here yet.</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
